As part of a grand plan designed by [[the Betrayer]], Demigorgan was disguised as [[Eathon Lambert]]'s [[Holotome]] and was planted by [[Rassimov]] in [[The Professor's castle]] for [[Lok Lambert]] to find. Lok immediately recognised the Holotome as Eathon's from when he was a child and used it to a make plan of attack against [[the Professor]]. {{source|The Mission}}

When the Huntik team discovered the [[Nexus]] in Peru and managed to contact [[Eathon Lambert]] in the [[Spirit World]], Demigorgan, as Eathon's Holotome, spied on them, learning Eathon's face and voice so as to impersonate him in the future. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}} Demigorgan then began to display messages from Eathon to Lok and the team, giving them clues and leading them to the [[Legendary Titans]] [[Umbra]] and [[Phoenix]], as [[the Betrayer]] knew that the Huntik team would not make it to the [[Spiral Mark]] without them. Faking the last prophecies of [[Nostradamus]], the Betrayer was able to trick Lok into driving the [[Willblade]] into the Spiral mark, breaking the seal that [[Lord Casterwill]] had put in place and signalling the return of the [[Nullifiers]]. {{source|The Spiral Mark}}

In the battle between the [[Blood Spiral]] and the [[Casterwill]]-[[Foundation]] alliance, Demigorgan was invoked by [[the Betrayer]] and was revealed to have been feeding information to the Huntik Foundation. When Zhalia tried to save Lok and Sophie from Demigorgan, it easily defeated her [[King Basilisk]]. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} Demigorgan fought against [[Den Fears|Den]] and [[Harrison Fears]] and their respective Titans, [[Dullahan]] and [[Jericho]], easily defeating Dullahan.

When [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] joined the fight, Demigorgan created copies of the Huntik team to send their Titans back to their Amulets and subsequently take on the forms of these Titans. These clones were defeated by Powerbonded [[Pendragon]], but a subsequent copy of the original [[Champion of Casterwill]] was able to subdue. However, Demigorgan was defeated by an empowered Lok, who destroyed its Amulet for good by channeling [[Quetzalcoatl]]'s energy through the [[Willblade]]. {{source|Dante's Return}}
